ID: vr-73
Title: Idle performance mode and quick head opacity
GitHub: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/72

Status: DONE
Milestone: Silent heads sleep visibly and resume on actual playback
Dependencies: vr-71

Purpose:
  Opt into 10% idle / 100% speaking opacity and suspend unnecessary idle work.
  Add normal opacity plus quick settings above every supported head.

Tasks:
  Isolate candidate source/profile/cache/backend from the protected live head.
  Gate RAF, blink/idle clocks and native cursor polling without losing choices.
  Keep menus usable; synchronize main/quick/manager controls.
  Exercise speech/pause/end/cancel/error and mode changes on real runtimes.
  Measure owned-process CPU and memory on/off, without moving the real cursor.
  Update authored docs, journal, tracking and owned continuity; deliver candidate.

Acceptance criteria:
  Enabled silent head is 10% opaque, speaking face/voice is 100%.
  Silent head ignores cursor and has no periodic gesture/blink/render work.
  Normal opacity is adjustable 0-100%; mode overrides it, never deletes it.
  Quick controls remain readable/recoverable even at zero head opacity.
  Speech clock/model/clip/control choices survive; disable restores normal use.
  Actual bounded A/B receipts distinguish CPU changes from retained warm memory.
  No camera/mic/cloud/download, unrelated runtime mutation or claimed accuracy.

Completion evidence:
  Final .local/qualification/idle-performance-final-01: six actual heads,
    four views each. Zero sleeping draws/uploads/storage/native cursor reads.
    Actual native alpha: 61,103 sampled pixels match 10% within two byte levels;
    menu remains opaque. Quick/manager controls and saved choices qualify.
  All six use decoded synthetic WAV playback/end. Real Claire face/voice agent
    preparation, advancing audio, mode changes during playback and cancellation
    qualify. Unit/media/controller, nine HTTP and nine book checks pass.
  Eight counterbalanced 16s windows, owned Electron CPU only, one-core scale:
    stationary 2.786% off / 0.305% on; moving 28.856% / 0.368%.
    Moving working-set mean 755.68 / 754.61 MiB; no substantial RAM claim.
    Model/clip remain warm. Not whole-machine/GPU-energy/listening acceptance.
  Candidate .local/worktrees/performance-73 shares pinned model/node_modules
    inputs (not OS-enforced read-only); fresh derived cache/profile/backend.
    Exact pinned authored MPFB reference copied locally; no download.
  .local/qualification/live-performance-01 saves fresh old settings. At
    2026-11-22T00:15:46+05:30, replace only old owned head289864 with306520;
    same manager293308, every old control/appearance preserved, performance
    enabled, normal opacity100. No replay or sibling restart. Twelve promoted
    files match qualified candidate. Owned test resources stopped.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Owner explicitly requests autonomous implementation and measured
    idle savings. Choose opt-in default, immediate sleep while not playing,
    no polling wakeup or idle CSS fade. Menus are not dimmed with the head.
  2026-11-22 - Implemented and environment-qualified; source/docs/journal
    updated. Retain initial harness failures (early screen API, multi-control
    transaction, fixed audio-start delay), missing authored-input attempt and
    their successful corrected runs. No weakened gate or guaranteed RAM saving.
